you would be hard-pressed to find many  folks who don't know indiana jones  nowadays the legacy of the indiana jones  films is enduring thanks in part to it  having no shortage of memorable moments  here are some of the most paused scenes  in the indiana jones movies  in the opening sequence of raiders of  the lost ark director steven spielberg  does an incredible job of letting us  know exactly what indiana jones is all  about there are puzzles traps betrayal  and a giant boulder hell-bent on  smushing our hero indy navigates a  sequence of deadly traps and arrives at  the treasure he seeks we're then left in  suspense as he stares down a grimacing  gold relic the moment hangs in the air  for longer than expected but rather than  the hesitation making us anxious we wait  patiently we trust that indy knows what  he's doing given that we only met this  man minutes earlier it's quite an  achievement plus we get to find out what  that sack full of sand is all about  indiana jones presents himself as a  fearless protagonist throughout the  entire film series however there's no  denying the fear in his eyes when faced  with a serpent  i hate snake shark i hate him  come on show a little bath bomb will ya  the temple which houses the titular ark  is crawling with the slithery devils a  setting befitting the dangerous power  contained within the ark of the covenant  andy hijacks a portion of the nazi dig  site in the desert once he discovers the  real location of the ark there's a  moment that follows when andy falls to  the ground and looks up to discover he's  face to face with a hissing cobra he  locks eyes with the creature before  scrambling away and in that moment you  see the normally stoic action hero have  a base of pure panic  even if you lock him in an ancient snake  riddled throne room that hasn't been  opened in thousands of years indiana  jones will still find an exit which in  this instance is also conveniently near  a nazi-occupied airstrip good thing too  because at this point in raiders it's  been far too long since we've seen  indiana engaged in fisticuffs  fortunately our lust for action is  satiated by a burly mustachioed nazi  who's eager for battle indy isn't always  the top dog in a fight but when he lacks  in fighting prowess he makes up for an  ingenuity his enemy in the scene looks  formidable but indy always manages to  find a clever way to overcome his  opponent however in this case defeating  this gladiator nazi on the airstrip is  entirely a matter of blind luck a series  of events that has to happen for this  final boss to go face first and airplane  propeller blades is fantastically silly  and truly a wonder to behold  the ark of the covenant is shrouded in  mystery for most of the first film we're  left in the dark as to what exactly is  contained within that beautiful gold  sarcophagus after indy combats nazis  across the globe for over 90 minutes  it's time for the final reveal of the  ark with all we have emotionally  invested in the journey what lies inside  that ancient tomb best be mind-blowing  and it lives up to that expectation when  marion is nabbed by the evil doers andy  trails them atop a submarine eventually  arriving in an isolated island india  doesn't do so well in foiling any plans  and winds up tied to a stake on a  mountaintop while the bad guys  ceremoniously open the ark what's  unleashed is an unholy wave of  destruction among the nazis as the  spirits whip around and annihilate  anything that looks at them a viewing  experience that continues to deliver the  goods over and over again  the opening scene of temple of doom had  a lot to live up to considering the now  iconic boulder chase scene in the first  film the second film in the series opens  with a glamorous show tune with lots of  sparkly dresses moments later instep's  indiana jones not clothed in his usual  leather jacket in fedora but in a fancy  white tuxedo there's an exchange taking  place between jones and some shady  characters we don't exactly know what's  being traded but that's not the point  the point is harrison ford looks sharp  and it's time for another adventure an  acknowledgment of a successful deal indy  lifts a glass of champagne and gulps it  down the bad men began cackling with  laughter because our hero just drank  poison the antidote is in an extremely  durable vial that winds up being kicked  around the dance floor while the entire  dining room erupts into chaos watching  indy scramble about chasing the vial  around the dance floor is a fun comical  experience  when indiana jones and the temple of  doom was released in 1984 there was no  such thing as a pg-13 rating thanks to  the nightmare fuel that was tossed on an  entire generation of kids who saw this  pg-rated installment of indiana jones  the motion picture association of  america decided to create a rating to  bridge the gap between pg and r ratings  in temple of doom circumstances result  in indiana and his companions being  stranded in india after a plane crash  all roads forced them to a society  housing a dark secret mostly a  mind-controlling shaman named mularam  who leads an army of acolytes with  aspirations of world domination and he  gets backrow seats to one of their  ceremonies and witnesses rom uses bare  hand to reach into a man's chest and  pull out his heart he then holds the  still-beating heart while the man  remains alive long enough to be lowered  into a lava pit as a man screams in  agony below the heart and rom's hand  bursts into flames it's a haunting image  that certainly warranted a  re-examination of our movie rating  system  in temple of doom indiana jones manages  to escape his captors in a wild mine  cart ride that feels like steven  spielberg's audition for disney world  the escape reaches a climactic moment  when indian pals are surrounded by the  baddies on a rope bridge extending over  a canyon a river teeming with crocodiles  lies several hundred feet below  out of safer options he offers up a  knowing glance to his sidekick short  round as he raises his sword to cut the  bridge he knows everyone including him  and his allies will be sent tumbling to  the cliffside along with the collapsing  bridge it seems extreme but staring  death in the face and smirking is just a  part of daily life for indiana jones oh  my god  oh my god  in the last crusade when indy finally  tracks down his abducted father's  location he's betrayed by his would-be  lover elsa the subtlety with which ford  and connery act out the realization they  both slept with the same woman as a  re-watchable moment all and of itself  here father and son end up being tied up  together as the nazis rummage through  all their research but the real fun  begins when connery fumbles a zippo  lighter and sends their lush prison up  in flames indiana's father are tied back  to back against some chairs and are  powerless to escape as the entire room  ignites into flames the two men hop  their way over to the fireplace to  escape the fire while frantically trying  to free himself from his restraint he  discovers that the fireplace has a  trapdoor leading to a nazi command room  not exactly the help they were hoping  for because the soldiers immediately  opened fire on them what follows is a  humorous sequence of events involving  deception and locking a bunch of nazis  in a makeshift furnace  it's not easy to pick just one moment  from this entire motorcycle chase in the  last crusade everything works together  beautifully to create an exciting  action-packed sequence that's also  modestly hilarious seeing the man who  defined james bond and a dorky hats and  glasses protecting his briefcase and  umbrella while refusing to acknowledge  his son's awesomeness speaks to the  essence of the last crusade indiana  jones and his father escape on a  motorcycle with a sidecar but their  would-be captors are in hot pursuit  after rolling through a barricade indy  grabs a flagpole and uses it as a lance  to knock an incoming nazi off his bike  the loose bike zips off and crashes into  several other pursuers the final  motorcycle batty is finished off when  indy uses the remaining fragment from  his makeshift lance and plunges it into  his enemies wheel spokes the only  acknowledgement he gets from his father  at this miraculous escape is an  expressionless face as he whines his  pocket watch typical  those pesky nazis always seem to find a  way to stay on indy's trail and bogart  any of his discoveries this time they  kidnap his father in an attempt to force  him to reveal the location of the holy  grail good thing henry jones jr can take  a punch and still think straight without  that presence of mind pops would be  squashed underneath the unforgiving  tread of a tank indy's father is being  kept inside a tank guarded by truckloads  of soldiers but andy blasts his way  through them all in order to help his  dad get out of the musty military  vehicle in a series of unfortunate  events papa jones falls onto the treads  and is about to be whisked off to his  death before indy pulls out his trusty  whip and latches it onto his father's  leg andy then has to hold on to the  weight of a full-grown man while a nazi  jerk pummels his kidneys it's an action  scene that proves indiana jones as the  alpha archaeologist  all roads lead indiana jones his  companions and their nazi captors to a  canyon housing a centuries-old temple  inside this temple is a series of booby  traps that can only be navigated with  decades of research and some quick  thinking behind all these contraptions  lies the holy grail the cup of christ is  known to be a source of immortality but  there are some caveats after water from  the cup heals henry jones senior's  gunshot wound the flip-flopping elsa  picks it up and begins excitedly  proclaiming that glory is theirs her  hubris causes her to forget the ancient  crusaders warning to never take the cup  past the temple seal the earth rumbles  and the ground breaks open to ultimately  send elsa falling to her doom india also  ends up falling into the same crevice  but his father grabs his hand at the  last moment the holy grail is barely out  of reach on an opposite ledge and indie  desperately reaches out outpour despite  his father's hands slipping connery  injects serenity into the chaos and  speaks softly indiana  let it go  it's a statement that carries an extreme  amount of weight it means father jones's  life's pursuit is meaningless next to  the life of his son  indiana jones in the kingdom of the  crystal skull had almost 20 years  between its release in 1989's the last  crusade and it was an absolute necessity  that we hit the ground running steven  spielberg made sure we got just that the  film opens in a government facility we  all recognize from the ending of the  first film a warehouse containing all  sorts of secrets the ark of the covenant  being one of them andy must not be very  good at choosing his friends because  he's betrayed once again by his  companion and forced to help the bad  guys find the treasure they seek andy  winds up escaping of course via a rocket  cart determined to shatter the land  speed record after that he ends up in a  small town which he slowly realizes is a  dummy town that's about to be on the  receiving end of a nuclear bomb test and  he hops inside a lead-lined refrigerator  and the blast launches him far away  where he stumbles out unscathed how  because he's indiana jones and we've  still got the rest of the movie to go  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite classic film franchises  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  you

